      "writtenOn": "2026-04-13T10:54:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem being handled is when the user does NOT specify --inject-scripts. Specifically, the issue with WPR assuming `deterministic.js` should always be injected.",
      "parentUuid": "db8ab9d9_ee272371",
      "revId": "42f327949bbf128f2a609a2b0780440cc25f8454",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d08b271_fd797691",
        "filename": "src/wpr.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 315,
      "author": {
        "id": 1328067
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-13T11:05:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How about just changing --inject-archive-scripts behavior to prefer scripts stored in the archive in case of conflict \n\nI\u0027d prefer not to do this. IMO a flag explicitly specified by the user should always override all other settings.",
      "parentUuid": "1649d115_be79b7fb",
      "revId": "42f327949bbf128f2a609a2b0780440cc25f8454",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24ca6f10_0e5ff5e9",
        "filename": "src/wpr.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 315,
      "author": {
        "id": 1339017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-13T11:27:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e a) This doesn\u0027t handle --inject-scripts\u003ddeterministic.js,foo.js\n\nOh, I see, the fix is specifically about the case when the --inject-scripts flag is omitted. Can you turn the `common.injectScripts \u003d\u003d \"deterministic.js\"` part into an assert then?\n\n\u003e I\u0027d prefer not to do this. IMO a flag explicitly specified by the user should always override all other settings\n\nThat\u0027s a fair point.\n\n\nIt\u0027s weird to me that --help claims --inject-scripts\u003ddeterministic.js and --inject-archive-scripts\u003dtrue by default but then if the user explicitly passes those same values they get a different behavior...  I don\u0027t think I can propose an alternative that\u0027s simple enough. Sad LGTM",
      "parentUuid": "7d08b271_fd797691",
      "revId": "42f327949bbf128f2a609a2b0780440cc25f8454",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7c6c101_d516c110",
        "filename": "src/wpr.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
